    <briefdescription>
<para>One bus node (master or slave) on top of the <ref refid="group__baton__link" kindref="compound">Link</ref>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The master passes the baton (POLL) to the slaves in a fixed order; only the polled slave transmits, for at most slot_time_ms, so the bus never has collisions. Messages are of two classes, defined by the application message lists in <computeroutput>baton_user_config.h</computeroutput>: <itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>EVENT: queued (HIGH or NORMAL priority), acknowledged, retransmitted, delivered exactly once and in order per (source, destination, priority), dropped after event_ttl_ms with an on_drop report; </para>
</listitem>
<listitem><para>STATE: a mailbox per state; the latest value is delivered to every other node, intermediate values may be skipped, it can never overflow.</para>
</listitem>
</itemizedlist>
Threading model: <ref refid="group__baton__node_1ga18e20ce4a3dc9bbee85f7f556d1dd92d" kindref="member">baton_node_init()</ref>, <ref refid="group__baton__node_1gad7b84e4390f7657c5fa0833613ba58d3" kindref="member">baton_node_process()</ref> and <ref refid="group__baton__node_1gacd6ae37a251cfa6478d268bc4a1262a2" kindref="member">baton_node_get_stats()</ref> run in one context (main loop or one RTOS task). <ref refid="group__baton__node_1gaef7ec0ea2f65edec2b84cd8d1ba4a952" kindref="member">baton_node_rx_isr()</ref> and <ref refid="group__baton__node_1ga633fade7c0d3118f38e1dae7258b52ae" kindref="member">baton_node_tx_done_isr()</ref> are called from the UART interrupts. <ref refid="group__baton__node_1ga3c8e0d35c10578eecc4089d0c979d9db" kindref="member">baton_node_send()</ref> and <ref refid="group__baton__node_1ga67e9a7b575f73fb8a120ac21d20d34ea" kindref="member">baton_node_publish()</ref> may be called from any context only when enter_critical and exit_critical are configured.</para>
<para>All memory is inside struct <ref refid="structbaton__node" kindref="compound">baton_node</ref>, owned by the caller. No function blocks, allocates memory or reads a clock.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Public interface includes:</title><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Lifecycle: <ref refid="group__baton__node_1ga97ee9e4ac3ab2acf286a664b0e0c97ef" kindref="member">baton_node_default_config</ref>, <ref refid="group__baton__node_1ga18e20ce4a3dc9bbee85f7f556d1dd92d" kindref="member">baton_node_init</ref>. </para>
</listitem>
<listitem><para>Processing: <ref refid="group__baton__node_1gad7b84e4390f7657c5fa0833613ba58d3" kindref="member">baton_node_process</ref>. </para>
</listitem>
<listitem><para>Messages: <ref refid="group__baton__node_1ga3c8e0d35c10578eecc4089d0c979d9db" kindref="member">baton_node_send</ref>, <ref refid="group__baton__node_1ga67e9a7b575f73fb8a120ac21d20d34ea" kindref="member">baton_node_publish</ref>. </para>
</listitem>
<listitem><para>Interrupt entry points: <ref refid="group__baton__node_1gaef7ec0ea2f65edec2b84cd8d1ba4a952" kindref="member">baton_node_rx_isr</ref>, <ref refid="group__baton__node_1ga633fade7c0d3118f38e1dae7258b52ae" kindref="member">baton_node_tx_done_isr</ref>. </para>
</listitem>
<listitem><para>Diagnostics: <ref refid="group__baton__node_1gacd6ae37a251cfa6478d268bc4a1262a2" kindref="member">baton_node_get_stats</ref>. </para>
</listitem>
</itemizedlist>
</para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
